\section{Anharmonic Mass Spectrum}

The KK masses follow from the eigenvalue equation
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}[fn] = mn^2 f_n,
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{L}$ is the Sturm--Liouville operator defined in
Eq.~(\ref{eq:SL}). The anharmonic contribution modifies the effective potential
and shifts the eigenvalues.

The full mass spectrum is
\begin{equation}
m_n^2 =
4k^2
+ 2\sqrt{\lambda}\left(n+\tfrac{1}{2}\right)
+ \frac{12\lambda_4}{16\lambda^2}
\left( 6n^2 + 6n + 3 \right).
\label{eq:full_mass}
\end{equation}

The deviation from RS equidistance is quantified by
\begin{equation}
\delta{12} = \frac{m2}{m_1} - 2, \qquad
\delta{23} = \frac{m3}{m2} - \frac{m2}{m_1}.
\end{equation}

